"ws-header wst-header-structure wst-unknown wst-header ws-header ws-noexport noprint dynlayout-exempt\"><div class=\"wst-header-mainblock wst-unknown-mainblock headertemplate\"><div class=\"wst-header-back searchaux wst-unknown-back\"><div class=\"wst-header-back-arrow\">←</div><div class=\"wst-header-back-link\"><a href=\"/wiki/Consider_the_Consequences!/S-23\" title=\"Consider the Consequences!/S-23\">S-23</a></div></div><div class=\"wst-header-central-cell wst-unknown-central-cell\"><span class=\"wst-header-title wst-unknown-title\"><span class=\"wst-header-title-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Consider_the_Consequences!\" title=\"Consider the Consequences!\">Consider the Consequences!</a></span><div class=\"header-section-text\">S-24</div></span></div><div class=\"wst-header-forward searchaux wst-unknown-forward\"><div class=\"wst-header-forward-link\"><a href=\"/wiki/Consider_the_Consequences!/S-25\" title=\"Consider the Consequences!/S-25\">S-25</a></div><div class=\"wst-header-forward-arrow\">→</div></div></div><div class=\"ws-noexport\" id=\"ws-data\" style=\"speak:none\"><span id=\"ws-article-id\">5009465</span><span id=\"ws-title\"><a href=\"/wiki/Consider_the_Consequences!\" title=\"Consider the Consequences!\">Consider the Consequences!</a> — S-24</span></div></div>\n<div class=\"prp-pages-output\" lang=\"en\">\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15621227/mw-parser-output/.prp-pages-output\">.mw-parser-output .prp-pages-output .__pagefooter{font-size:smaller}</style><span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"173\" data-page-number=\"173\" data-page-name=\"Page:Consider the Consequences! (IA consider-the-consequences-1930).djvu/178\" data-page-index=\"178\" data-page-quality=\"4\" title=\"Page:Consider&#95;the&#95;Consequences!&#95;(IA&#95;consider-the-consequences-1930).djvu/178\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;178\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15620827\">.mw-parser-output .wst-center{text-align:center;margin:0 auto}.mw-parser-output .wst-center.wst-center-nomargin>p{margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0}</style><div class=\"wst-center tiInherit\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size:120%;\">S-24</span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"wst-dhr\" style=\"visibility:hidden; line-height:100%;\">&#160;</div>\n<p><span class=\"smallcaps\" style=\"font-variant:small-caps;\">Saunders</span> tried to break off tactfully with Ada when he saw that she wanted to marry him, but he had not reckoned with the tenacity of her nature. She bombarded him with telephone calls, sent him broken-hearted little notes, and finally appealed to his mother and Marge. The effect of all this was to confirm Saunders in his opinion that Ada was not the right wife for him.\n</p><p>But Ada had resources. When Saunders finally consented to go to her home for one last interview she greatly embarrassed him by going down on her knees to him and begging him to forgive her for whatever it was she had done to offend him. When he started to leave, she had violent hysterics and declared that she would kill herself. Her mother rushed in and Saunders made his escape.\n</p><p>Next morning it was all over town that poor Ada had locked herself in her room and turned on the gas, and her frightened parents had had a hard time to persuade her to unlock the door. After this they sent her to make a long visit to a relative in a Western city, where she married a Spaniard, writing back to her parents that it was a case of love at first sight. Saunders sent her a beautiful wedding&#32;<span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"174\" data-page-number=\"174\" data-page-name=\"Page:Consider the Consequences! (IA consider-the-consequences-1930).djvu/179\" data-page-index=\"179\" data-page-quality=\"4\" title=\"Page:Consider&#95;the&#95;Consequences!&#95;(IA&#95;consider-the-consequences-1930).djvu/179\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;179\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span>gift and married a darned nice, sensible, plain, intelligent girl. For a while he was jumpy whenever an impatient word or praise of another woman slipped out of his mouth, but when he found that his wife was not sensitive like Ada, he settled down to be comfortable with her and continued to be comfortable.\n</p><p>The consequence was that the children brought up in this harmonious atmosphere had no nerves but much intelligence and health and joy in living. The Saunders family was a normal American family—the kind authors are always being asked to write about but can't, because the essence of drama is conflict, and there is no conflict in this sort of family.\n</p>\n<div class=\"&#95;&#95;nop wst-nop\"></div>\n<p>&#32;\n</p>\n</div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nParsed by mw‐api‐ext.eqiad.main‐77f8cc8f9b‐db5k4\nCached time: 20260920184856\nCache expiry: 2592000\nCache expiry source: Module:Header (os.date(%Y))\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [vary‐page‐id, vary‐revision‐sha1]\nCPU time usage: 0.122 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.224 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 185/1000000\nRevision size: 275/2097152 bytes\nPost‐expand include size: 6151/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 1040/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 11/100\nExpensive parser function count: 1/500\nUnstrip recursion depth: 1/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5441/5000000 bytes\nLua time usage: 0.059/10.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 1032558/52428800 bytes\nNumber of Wikibase entities loaded: 0/500\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%  214.743      1 -total\n 52.16%  112.019      1 Template:Header\n 32.51%   69.815      1 Page:Consider_the_Consequences!_(IA_consider-the-consequences-1930).djvu/178\n 16.32%   35.045      1 Template:C\n  7.18%   15.409      1 Template:Center/s\n  3.42%    7.335      2 Template:Optional_style\n  3.18%    6.825      1 Template:Sc\n  2.57%    5.522      1 Template:Larger\n  2.49%    5.343      1 Template:Center/e\n  2.04%    4.380      1